## Context

Commits 55a8548 and f37be87 landed the v0 pipeline design into
`slides/slides.tex` (fusion reframe, fragment taxonomy, incrementality,
sidecar + invariants, 3-tier verification with HITL memory, agents
anchored on data-model concerns). The content is correct; the
finalization gaps are cosmetic and linguistic.

## Scope

### 1. Layout — overfull vbox warnings

Clean build against parent commit `13d53d5`: 19 overfull/underfull
warnings. After the sync: 80 warnings (+61). Offending frames
(height overflow, in points past boundary):

| Line | Frame | Overflow |
|---|---|---|
| 207 | Why not just verify the output? | 118 pt |
| 683 | Local model scaling: RAG lifts all sizes | 94 pt |
| 1117 | From pilot to production pipeline | 87 pt |
| 841 | The cost of trust | 72 pt |
| 481 | Pilot: Vietnam thermal plant extraction | 71 pt |
| 562, 409, 349, 305 | Baseline / Epistemic / Incrementality / Fragment taxonomy | 24–64 pt |

Four of these are new frames introduced by the v0 sync (fragment
taxonomy, incrementality, v0 data model, epistemic accountability).
Each needs density reduction: split the frame, shrink font, prune
bullets, or reduce column widths. Overfull vbox = content clips off
the projected slide, not just a warning.

### 2. French translation

The talk is in French (Econom'IA, Thema / Cergy). The deck is
currently in English. All new slide content — the five fusion /
taxonomy / incrementality / sidecar / epistemic-accountability
frames plus the two verification-tier frames plus the rewritten
architecture frame — needs translation. The pre-existing frames
(problem statement, pilot design, RAG results, cost-quality,
takeaway) also need translation to match.

Pattern: keep source slides.tex in one language end-to-end. Either
translate in place, or fork to `slides_fr.tex` and maintain both.
Author preference unknown — ask before choosing.

### 3. Tier numbering reconciliation (slides vs MASTERPLAN)

Slides frame 844 ("Verification at scale: three tiers") shows **four**
rows labeled 0–3, where tier 0 is "diff audit: only changed cells
need verification." MASTERPLAN §"Three-tier verification with
audit-verified HITL memory" describes **three** tiers and frames the
diff audit as a pre-filter applied *before* tier 1.

Both framings are defensible; pick one and make both artifacts agree.
Recommendation: keep MASTERPLAN's three-tier framing (the name is in
the title of ticket 0097), rename slides row "0" to "Pre-filter" or
move it into a separate preamble line above the three-row table. No
content change — only the numbering label.

## Test

Build check:
- `make slides` produces `slides.pdf`.
- Overfull vbox warnings on the target frames ≤ 0 pt
  (the other overfull warnings are pre-existing, not in scope).
- All slide content is in French; no English bold tokens in new frames.
- No row labeled "0" in the verification-tier table; the diff audit is
  described as a pre-filter matching MASTERPLAN.

Content-level checks (visual review):
- Rehearse the talk from the PDF: all text legible, nothing clipped.
- Quoted examples (Vietnamese, e.g. "Công suất lắp đặt", "Nhóm")
  render correctly.

## Exit criteria

- Zero new overfull vbox warnings on the 9 offending frames (other
  warnings may remain if pre-existing).
- Slides fully in French.
- Tier numbering consistent between slides and MASTERPLAN.
- `slides.pdf` committed; `make slides` green.
- Visual walk-through with the author signed off.
